@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<div class="privacy-page">

    <div class="privacy-header">
        <span class="section-label">PRIVACY</span>

        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

        <p>
            This page explains how information is used within the
            Lost & Found Platform.
        </p>
    </div>


    <div class="privacy-card">

        <section>
            <h2>Information we collect</h2>

            <p>
                The platform stores the information users provide when
                creating an account, adding items, publishing lost or
                found reports, creating locations and sending messages.
            </p>
        </section>


        <section>
            <h2>Account information</h2>

            <p>
                Users register with an email address and password.
                Account information is used to identify users and allow
                them to manage their own items, reports, locations and
                conversations.
            </p>
        </section>


        <section>
            <h2>Lost and found reports</h2>

            <p>
                Information entered in lost and found reports may be
                visible to other users of the platform. This can include
                item descriptions, locations and report details.
            </p>
        </section>


        <section>
            <h2>Messages</h2>

            <p>
                Messages exchanged through the platform are stored so
                users can communicate about a specific lost or found item.
                Conversations are available only to the users participating
                in them.
            </p>
        </section>


        <section>
            <h2>Location information</h2>

            <p>
                Locations are entered manually by users and are used to
                describe where an item was lost, found or can be picked up.
                Users should avoid entering unnecessary private information.
            </p>
        </section>


        <section>
            <h2>Data management</h2>

            <p>
                Users can manage the items, reports and locations they
                create. Certain records cannot be deleted while they are
                still being used by other parts of the platform.
            </p>
        </section>


        <section>
            <h2>About this platform</h2>

            <p>
                Lost & Found Platform is a demonstration web application
                developed as an educational project using ASP.NET Core MVC
                and ASP.NET Core Identity.
            </p>
        </section>

    </div>

</div>